Can you run subagents?
Worked for 26s
Not in the usual sense. This session does not expose a generic "spawn subagent" tool that lets me launch separate autonomous model instances, choose their models, assign tasks, and collect their reports.
I can still:
• issue several independent tool calls in parallel;
• use specialized tools and connected services;
• divide a problem into separate workstreams and synthesize the results myself;
• run subprocesses in the container, though those are ordinary programs-not LLM agents.
So I can imitate some benefits of subagents through parallel tool use, but I cannot currently create true delegated LLM workers from this chat.
